  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Bing Sai Chuan identifies the hill-like tiger blocking Calamity Luck Altar as a Shabi, a monster formed in the fiendish qi sea spring. With qi path going extinct and that spring gone, this is the only Shabi left. Seven Fiendish Primeval Monarch nurtured it in the Olden Antiquity Era among ninety-nine Shabi. It was one of the last few created, number ninety-five; Giant Sun later named it Shabi Ninety-five when invited to Heavenly Court. It resides in Eternal Sand Cave, fights with a sandstorm, and displays peak rank eight battle strength. Heavenly Court has three legendary immemorial beasts: Shabi Ninety-five, Ruan Dan, and Cang Xuan Zi.",
      "chapters": [
        1712
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_bing_sai_chuan",
        "house_calamity_luck_altar",
        "char_seven_fiendish_primeval_monarch",
        "evt_era_olden",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "loc_eternal_sand_cave",
        "char_ruan_dan",
        "char_cang_xuan_zi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "It looks like a tiger but is a Shabi: overwhelming aura, a body that seems made of metal, golden skin, silver teeth, ruby-like eyes, and a forehead marking of sand rather than the usual king character. It speaks human words.",
      "chapters": [
        1712
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is shocked to recognize Mao Li Qiu, then is pressed down and argues about age and who should be called grandfather. While Ruan Dan is slammed by Mao Li Qiu, it laughs and tries to leave for Five Deity Hall, but a clone with equal strength pins it. It likes pouncing on others from above and treats being underneath as humiliation.",
      "chapters": [
        1712
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fight-with-mao-li-qiu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_mao_li_qiu",
        "loc_five_deity_hall"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "It grabs Mao Li Qiu’s hind leg and bites during continued fighting.",
      "chapters": [
        1722
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "hind-leg-bite",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "At a crucial moment it emerges with a tiger roar beside Ruan Dan as Heavenly Court’s legendary immemorial beasts.",
      "chapters": [
        1934
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-book-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Qin Ding Ling names it with Ruan Dan among Heavenly Court’s three legendary immemorial beasts.",
      "chapters": [
        1938
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-book-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_qin_ding_ling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Zhan Bu Du keeps killing Ruan Dan, it rushes to help a friend despite ordinary arguments between them, then takes a heavy blow from Demon Immortal Qi Jue and falls from the sky.",
      "chapters": [
        2180
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-and-book-mountain",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_zhan_bu_du",
        "char_demon_immortal_qi_jue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Seven Fiendish Primeval Monarch beckons it as Ninety-five. It answers as master with admiration and fear, then is mostly healed by a light petting.",
      "chapters": [
        2181
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "master-and-healing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Facing Demon Immortal Qi Jue again, its qi path killer move is absorbed by damaged Xi Land, and it retreats in fright.",
      "chapters": [
        2191
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "qi-path-killer-move",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_xi_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Seven Fiendish Primeval Monarch attacks while riding it; after Qi Jue and Shen Shang kill the master, it is hacked into two and dies on the spot.",
      "chapters": [
        2198
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death-beside-its-master",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_shen_shang"
      ]
    }
  ],
